<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hornus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		contr. for hōrinus = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρινος</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of this year</i>, <i>this year's</i>
			(not in Cic.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">but cf. hornotinus): agni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			, (5), 3, 61: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fruge,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 23, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Epod. 2, 47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					S. 2, 6, 88</span></i>
			. —<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">horno</span></b> , <i>this year</i>: utrum
			anno an horno te abstuleris a viro? Lucil. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 121, 8</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">horno messis magna fuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Most. 1, 3, 3</span></i>
			; Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 121,
		10</span></i>.</div>
